graphify-out/
.joca/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/
# Working memory — THIS REPO IS PUBLIC (github.com/MirrasPT/JOCA).
# decisions/learnings/checkpoints were already covered; knowledge/projects/feedback were not,
# and those are exactly where /know and /save write. A client PDF ingested by /know, or a /start
# in a private project, would land in the public repo with nothing to stop it.
memory/decisions/
memory/learnings/
memory/checkpoints/
memory/.index/
memory/knowledge/
memory/projects/*
memory/feedback/*

# Exceptions: memory about JOCA ITSELF — the toolkit documents itself and that is public.
# Memory about ANY OTHER project stays out by default; to share one you have to add it here
# deliberately.
!memory/projects/.gitkeep
!memory/projects/JOCA.md
!memory/feedback/.gitkeep
# Note: git keeps tracking files that are ALREADY tracked, even when covered by these rules — that
# is the case of feedback/archive/session-2026-07-30-20-31.md, which is about JOCA itself. If you
# ever archive feedback from a client project and it shows up in `git status`, it is because it was
# already tracked: `git rm --cached <file>` removes it from the repo without deleting it from disk.
.playwright-mcp/
/*.png
